<title>INDIA: Indian gold, silver prices fall on world trends.</title>
<headline>Indian gold, silver prices fall on world trends.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indian gold and silver prices fell in early trade on Tuesday on world trends, dealers said.</p>
<p>Physical demand was low and volumes were poor.</p>
<p>&quot;Weak world market trends led to the fall in the landing cost of imported metals,&quot; one broker said.</p>
<p>Prices of a gold biscuit (116.50 grammes) were unchanged at 59,800 rupees per piece, against a rise of 50 rupees on Monday.</p>
<p>The local bullion markets are closed on Wednesday for Mahatma Gandhi's birth anniversary.</p>
<p>They reopen on Thursday.</p>
